
# OpenTelemetry OTLP log export (opt-in). Standard OTel variable names, resolved by
# otel-log-emitter.ts (never by the vendor SDK reading process.env on its own in a browser
# build — see that file's module docstring). Leave OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT empty to opt
# out: with no endpoint, otel-log-emitter.ts never imports @opentelemetry/* and never sends a
# byte over the network; the base LogEmitter (CONSOLE_EMITTER / NULL_EMITTER) is unaffected.
# ⚠️ MEASURED 2026-09: the JS Logs signal is "not yet stable" upstream (Traces/Metrics are
# further along) — see otel-log-emitter.ts's module docstring for the source and the
# fire-and-forget rationale that follows from it.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
# Defaults to "unknown_service" upstream when left blank; name it after the project.
OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=
# Comma-separated key=value pairs, e.g. "authorization=Bearer <token>". Never commit a real
# value here — this file ships as .env.example too.
# ⚠️ SET THIS AND THE ENDPOINT MUST BE https:// (or loopback). These headers are how a
# provider's API key is carried, and OTLP/HTTP sends them in cleartext over http:// —
# otel-log-emitter.ts REFUSES to start the exporter in that case and warns, rather than
# leaking the credential to anything on the path.
# ⚠️ react-spa-webpack ONLY: anything shipped to the browser bundle is PUBLIC — webpack's
# DefinePlugin inlines every .env key as a literal into dist/. Never put a real provider
# credential here for that skeleton. Point OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT at a same-origin
# collector proxy that holds the real credential server-side instead, and leave this blank —
# the proxy needs no client-supplied header, and CORS on that proxy must accept the app's
# origin. ts-lib (Node) has no such constraint; a real credential there is as safe as any other
# server-side secret.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=
# Both variables above have signal-specific forms — OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_ENDPOINT and
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_HEADERS — which OVERRIDE the generic ones for logs. Set one of
# those instead if logs go somewhere other than traces/metrics; otel-log-emitter.ts honours
# the same precedence the OTel spec defines.
